      // SPACE in `지 마`, which misses the spec's own boundary example
      // ("…열지 말라고 명시", `03` A08). `지\s*말` and `-지 말-` forms are added so
      // a prohibition on a specific act is recognised as a boundary, not a taste.
      // The patterns are anchored to a PROHIBITION OF AN ACT rather than to any
      // negative verb, so an ordinary taste statement does not fall in here.
      if (/(하지\s*마|지\s*마|지\s*말|말라고|하지\s*말|원하지\s*않|않도록|않게|경계선|boundary|do not|don't\s+want)/i.test(raw)) return 'boundary';
